= unused client certificates: CertificateRequest is never sent; a client Certificate or CertificateVerify is an "other" handshake message and is refused with unexpected_message

@ 4.4.2.2
> - The certificate type MUST be X.509v3 [RFC5280], unless explicitly negotiated otherwise (e.g., [RFC7250]).
= code send every certificate of the chain file as an X.509 cert_data entry and never negotiate another certificate type
= test a_whole_handshake_and_data_both_ways
= test our_messages_are_well_formed
= deviation the X.509 version of the configured certificates is not checked: PLAN 5 "no X.509 parsing"; left to the operator's file
> - The server's end-entity certificate's public key (and associated restrictions) MUST be compatible with the selected authentication algorithm from the client's "signature_algorithms" extension (currently RSA, ECDSA, or EdDSA).
= code sign only with ecdsa_secp256r1_sha256, refuse a ClientHello that does not offer it, and fail startup unless the P-256 public key of the private key occurs in the leaf certificate
= test a_whole_handshake_and_data_both_ways
