= test alerts_from_the_client
= row step open whole even strict protected:alert => closed whole even strict
> Unknown Alert types MUST be treated as error alerts.
= code map every received alert description other than close_notify, known or unknown, to the alert event
= test alerts_from_the_client
= row step open whole even strict protected:alert => closed whole even strict
> Peers which receive a message which cannot be parsed according to the syntax (e.g., have a length extending beyond the message boundary or contain an out-of-range length) MUST terminate the connection with a "decode_error" alert.
= code fail with decode_error when a handshake message or an extension does not parse: a length running past its container, an out-of-range length, trailing bytes
= test what_is_refused_and_with_which_alert
= test bug_trailing_bytes_in_list_extensions_were_accepted
= test bytes_past_the_extensions_or_an_extension
