= row step open whole even strict invalid:decode_error => closed whole even strict alert:decode_error
> Peers which receive a message which is syntactically correct but semantically invalid (e.g., a DHE share of p - 1, or an invalid enum) MUST terminate the connection with an "illegal_parameter" alert.
= code fail with illegal_parameter when a message parses but its content is not allowed, e.g. a KeyUpdate whose request_update is neither 0 nor 1, or a ClientHello whose legacy_compression_methods is not exactly one zero byte
= test what_is_refused_and_with_which_alert
= test key_updates_from_the_client
= row step start whole even strict invalid:illegal_parameter => closed whole even strict alert:illegal_parameter
= row step open whole even strict invalid:illegal_parameter => closed whole even strict alert:illegal_parameter

@ 6.1
> Any data received after a closure alert has been received MUST be ignored.
= row step open whole even strict protected:close_notify => closed whole even strict alert:close_notify
= row step closed whole even strict protected:data => closed whole even strict
= check Handshake.ClosedIsFinal
> This alert SHOULD be followed by a "close_notify".
= unused user_canceled: shioko never sends it (it is not in the spec's Alerts set); one received is the generic alert event and closes the connection at once, without waiting for a close_notify
> Any data received after a closure alert has been received MUST be ignored.
= row step open whole even strict protected:close_notify => closed whole even strict alert:close_notify
= row step closed whole even strict protected:data => closed whole even strict
= check Handshake.ClosedIsFinal
> Each party MUST send a "close_notify" alert before closing its write side of the connection, unless it has already sent some error alert.
= row step open whole even strict close:- => closed whole even strict alert:close_notify
= row step start whole even strict close:- => closed whole even strict alert:close_notify
= row step open whole even strict protected:close_notify => closed whole even strict alert:close_notify
= code feed the close event, which sends close_notify, when the application is done, on every deadline and when the client's stream ends; the lost event, which sends nothing, is only for a failed transport that cannot be written to any more (PLAN section 5)
= test bug_close_notify_was_missing_on_shutdown
= test the_end_of_the_client_stream_is_answered
= test the_handshake_has_a_deadline
= deviation PLAN 5, known departures: ending at once while the other thread of a tunnel is blocked writing to the client sends no close_notify, since the record being written can neither be finished nor interleaved
> If the application protocol using TLS provides that any data may be carried over the underlying transport after the TLS connection is closed, the TLS implementation MUST receive a "close_notify" alert before indicating end-of-data to the application layer.
= unused carrying data over the transport after TLS has closed: shioko shuts the socket down when the TLS connection ends, so nothing ever follows on it

@ 6.2
> Upon transmission or receipt of a fatal alert message, both parties MUST immediately close the connection.
= check Handshake.AlertCloses
= check Handshake.AlertIsLast
= row step open whole even strict protected:alert => closed whole even strict
