= deviation PLAN section 5, known departures: secrets are overwritten when no longer needed, but without unsafe code the compiler is free to drop such writes, so erasure is not guaranteed

@ 7.2
> Once client_/server_application_traffic_secret_N+1 and its associated traffic keys have been computed, implementations SHOULD delete client_/server_application_traffic_secret_N and its associated traffic keys.
= code on every KeyUpdate replace the traffic secret, key and IV of that direction in place, so generation N is no longer held once N+1 is installed
= test the_next_generation_starts_over
= check Handshake.KeysMoveForward
= deviation PLAN section 5, known departures: the old secret and keys are overwritten, but without unsafe code the compiler is free to drop such writes

@ 7.4.2
> Note that this octet string ("Z" in IEEE 1363 terminology) as output by FE2OSP (the Field Element to Octet String Conversion Primitive) has constant length for any given field; leading zeros found in this octet string MUST NOT be truncated.
= unused ECDH over secp256r1, secp384r1 and secp521r1: only X25519 is implemented; key shares for other groups are skipped, and a ClientHello that lacks X25519 is refused with handshake_failure (PLAN section 5)
