= test what_is_refused_and_with_which_alert
= test refused_hellos_get_the_alert_of_the_plan
= test what_our_first_records_look_like
= code send key_share in ServerHello (our X25519 share) and in HelloRetryRequest (selected group x25519 only)
= test our_hellos_field_by_field
= test a_hello_retry_request_and_then_the_handshake
= row step start whole even strict invalid:missing_extension => closed whole even strict alert:missing_extension
= row step start whole even strict plain:hello_retry => retry whole even strict send:retry send:ccs
> - "pre_shared_key" is REQUIRED for PSK key agreement.
= unused PSK key agreement: offered PSKs are ignored and a full handshake follows; pre_shared_key anywhere but last in the ClientHello gets illegal_parameter (PLAN section 5)
> - "psk_key_exchange_modes" is REQUIRED for PSK key agreement.
= unused PSK key agreement: offered PSKs are ignored and a full handshake follows; pre_shared_key without psk_key_exchange_modes gets missing_extension (PLAN section 5)
> Such a ClientHello message MUST meet the following requirements:
= peer client: refused with missing_extension when signature_algorithms or key_share is absent (PLAN section 5); the cases that turn on supported_groups are not settled, see the gap two sentences below
= row step start whole even strict invalid:missing_extension => closed whole even strict alert:missing_extension
> - If not containing a "pre_shared_key" extension, it MUST contain both a "signature_algorithms" extension and a "supported_groups" extension.
= peer client: without signature_algorithms, refused with missing_extension, with or without pre_shared_key since PSKs are ignored (PLAN section 5); without supported_groups, not settled, see the gap two sentences below
= row step start whole even strict invalid:missing_extension => closed whole even strict alert:missing_extension
> - If containing a "supported_groups" extension, it MUST also contain a "key_share" extension, and vice versa.
= peer client: supported_groups without key_share is refused with missing_extension (PLAN section 5); key_share without supported_groups is not settled, see the gap in the next sentence
= row step start whole even strict invalid:missing_extension => closed whole even strict alert:missing_extension
> Servers receiving a ClientHello which does not conform to these requirements MUST abort the handshake with a "missing_extension" alert.
= code refuse with missing_extension a TLS 1.3 ClientHello, first or second, that lacks signature_algorithms or key_share (PLAN section 5)
= test what_is_refused_and_with_which_alert
= row step start whole even strict invalid:missing_extension => closed whole even strict alert:missing_extension
= row step retry whole even strict invalid:missing_extension => closed whole even strict alert:missing_extension
= code refuse a ClientHello that lacks signature_algorithms, supported_groups or key_share with missing_extension
= test what_is_refused_and_with_which_alert
= test refused_hellos_get_the_alert_of_the_plan
> Additionally, all implementations MUST support the use of the "server_name" extension with applications capable of using it.
